<title>SENEGAL: Senegal to sell 49 pct of state electricity firm.</title>
<headline>Senegal to sell 49 pct of state electricity firm.</headline>
<dateline>DAKAR 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Senegal is to sell 49 percent of the state electricity company SENELEC to a private company, with the state retaining the remaining 51 percent, energy minister Magued Diouf said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;The 49 percent will go to a strategic partner, a company that knows about electricity, with serious references,&quot; the minister told journalists. He did not name the partner.</p>
<p>SENELEC made an operating profit of 10.1 billion CFA francs ($17.4 million) in 1996 versus 9.5 billion in 1995.</p>
<p>($ = 580 CFA francs)</p>
</text>
